### Exercise 17: Applying MVC Pattern - Test Requests

### 1. Get all articles (via articleController.findAll)
GET http://localhost:3000/articles

### 2. Create an article (via articleController.create)
POST http://localhost:3000/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Applying MVC in Node.js and Express",
    "text": "Model-View-Controller pattern helps keep code clean and decoupled. Models manage database schemas, controllers handle business logic, and routers define endpoints.",
    "tags": ["NodeJS", "Express", "MVC", "Architecture"]
}

### 3. Get article by ID (via articleController.findById)
GET http://localhost:3000/articles/<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>

### 4. Update article by ID (via articleController.update)
PUT http://localhost:3000/articles/<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Mastering MVC Pattern in Express and Mongoose"
}

### 5. Create a comment for the article (via commentController.create)
POST http://localhost:3000/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "body": "Great explanation of the MVC pattern!",
    "article": "<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>"
}

### 6. Get all comments with populated article (via commentController.findAll)
GET http://localhost:3000/comments

### 7. Delete article by ID (via articleController.delete)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/articles/<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>
